{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1947","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1947","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1947\",\"parent_revision\":\"df0a828da8d5be9ec875403f21d65bf5618fbb8e44435956fdd2c0c564b91a41\",\"root_revision\":\"df0a828da8d5be9ec875403f21d65bf5618fbb8e44435956fdd2c0c564b91a41\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add claude code session transcript reader for live token/context observability in dispatch_wave_status** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/abtop.md \u2014 pattern: read-only file access to ~/.claude/sessions/ for token count, context window %, and live status\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Read Claude Code session JSONL transcripts to surface token/context data in dispatch_wave_status |\\n| dispatch_wave_status return shape | AVAILABLE | server.py line 4081; DispatchWaveSummary in models.py line 1468 \u2014 elapsed_seconds and cost present, no token fields |\\n| JSONL session file location | AVAILABLE | ~/.claude/projects/{git-slug}/*.jsonl; slug derivation verified in dh_paths.py line 278 |\\n| JSONL parsing precedent | AVAILABLE | health.py extract_actions and agent_last_actions already parse JSONL; usage fields from type=result events not currently extracted |\\n| type=result event schema | AVAILABLE | stream-json-protocol.md documents usage.input_tokens, usage.output_tokens, usage.cache_read_input_tokens, usage.cache_creation_input_tokens, total_cost_usd |\\n| Session-ID-to-JSONL-file linkage | MISSING | dispatch_wave_status knows pid of each item; PID to session_id mapping not stored anywhere in current pipeline |\\n| Context window limit source | PARTIAL | Model name available in dispatch plan but not in DispatchItemRecord |\\n| type=result accumulation semantics | MISSING | Sum all events vs use only last one not specified |\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen dispatch_wave_status(milestone=N, wave_num=W) is called while sessions are in-progress:\\n\\n1. For each in-progress item whose JSONL file is discoverable via session_id linkage, the response includes a token_snapshot with input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_creation_tokens, estimated_cost_usd, and optionally context_utilisation_pct.\\n2. Items whose JSONL file is not yet found return token_snapshot: null.\\n3. For completed items, the token snapshot reflects the cumulative usage from type=result events.\\n4. When the JSONL directory does not exist, the tool returns without error \u2014 token fields are absent or null, existing fields are unaffected.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- DispatchItemRecord in backlog_core/models.py gains optional fields: session_id, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_creation_tokens, estimated_cost_usd, context_pct.\\n- A new function read_session_transcript_usage in backlog_core/ reads the JSONL file and returns a cumulative usage snapshot from all type=result events.\\n- dispatch_wave_status calls the reader for each item and populates the new fields before returning.\\n- The SQLite items table gains a session_id column (migration via ALTER TABLE IF NOT EXISTS in ensure_schema).\\n- _run_spawn_item in server.py is updated to extract session_id from spawn.py output JSON and store it.\\n- health.py's jsonl_dir_for_project() function or equivalent logic is reused for path resolution.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. dispatch_wave_status(milestone=N, wave_num=W) returns items with input_tokens and output_tokens fields (nullable when JSONL not yet available) \u2014 verifiable by calling the tool after spawning at least one item.\\n2. uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/ -k dispatch_wave_status passes with new test coverage for the token-snapshot path, including the case where JSONL directory is absent.\\n3. When the JSONL directory does not exist, dispatch_wave_status returns without an error key and with token_snapshot: null for all items.\\n4. The SQLite items table gains a session_id column: verifiable via `sqlite3 ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/dispatch-state.db '.schema items'` showing session_id TEXT.\\n5. uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ && uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ exits 0.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should dispatch_wave_status only surface token snapshots from JSONL, or also expose tmux pane content \u2014 or are those separate items?\\n- Does spawn.py already emit a session_id in its stdout JSON? (If not, that field must be added to _DispatchSpawnResult and _run_spawn_item.)\\n- Should the wave-level summary aggregate totals (wave_total_input_tokens, wave_total_cost_usd) or only expose per-item snapshots?\\n- When claude -p is used, does a JSONL session file get written to ~/.claude/projects/{slug}/? Confirm JSONL files are written for claude -p invocations.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:kage-bunshin |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/health.py \u2014 extract_actions, jsonl_dir_for_project |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py \u2014 DispatchStateManager, schema, check_stale_pids |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py \u2014 dispatch_wave_status, _run_spawn_item |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py \u2014 DispatchItemRecord, DispatchWaveSummary |\\n| Reference | plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/references/stream-json-protocol.md \u2014 JSONL event schema |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None identified \u2014 self-contained enhancement to an existing tool\\n- Blocks: Any cost/observability dashboard work relying on token data from dispatch_wave_status\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Session-ID-to-JSONL-file linkage strategy is UNVERIFIED: must confirm whether spawn.py stdout JSON already emits a session_id field before implementation can begin\\n- type=result event accumulation semantics (last event only vs. sum all) must be decided before implementing the reader\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 3-5 focused implementation sessions. The JSONL parsing pattern is established by health.py. Primary work: (1) verifying and adding session_id linkage in dispatch lifecycle, (2) implementing transcript_reader.py, (3) extending DispatchItemRecord and SQLite schema, (4) writing test coverage.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py | Add optional fields to DispatchItemRecord and DispatchWaveSummary |\\n| plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py | Add session_id column to SQLite schema; add set_item_session_id method |\\n| plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py | Update dispatch_wave_status to call transcript reader; update _run_spawn_item to capture session_id |\\n| plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/transcript_reader.py (new) | JSONL parsing function returning cumulative usage snapshot |\\n| plugins/development-harness/tests/ | New test coverage for transcript reader and dispatch_wave_status token fields |\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\ntype=result event accumulation semantics (last event only vs. sum all) must be decided before implementing the reader. The session-ID-to-JSONL-file linkage strategy must be verified: confirm whether spawn.py stdout JSON already emits a session_id field before implementation begins (check spawn.py spawn subcommand output JSON schema around lines 125-135).\\n\\nJSONL parsing pattern is established by health.py and can be adapted directly. No architectural novelty.\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an orchestrator agent running /dh:work-milestone, I want dispatch_wave_status to surface live token consumption, context window utilisation, cache hit rates, and per-turn cost for each in-progress kage-bunshin session so that I can detect runaway sessions, rebalance waves, and make informed decisions about when to intervene \u2014 without polling tmux panes or waiting for sessions to complete.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/monitor.py` only knows about kage-bunshin's own registry file at `_registry_path()` (lines 127-145). It does not parse `~/.claude/sessions/*/transcript.jsonl` or `~/.claude/projects/*/` files. Token counts, context-window utilization, and current-task fields exist in those Claude-Code-internal transcript files but the dh plugin does not read them. Live session token consumption per kage-bunshin child is therefore not observable to the orchestrator.\\n\\nSymptom: `dispatch_wave_status` reports per-item `status` and `cost` (set by `dispatch_item_status` on completion) but cannot show in-flight token usage. A wave orchestrator deciding whether to dispatch the next batch has no signal that running items are about to hit the context window.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new `plugins/development-harness/scripts/claude_session_reader.py` (read-only, no writes) parses `~/.claude/sessions/{session_id}/transcript.jsonl` for a given session ID and returns `{token_count, context_window_pct, current_tool, last_message_at}`. `monitor.py` calls it on slow ticks (every 5 ticks, 10s) and merges the result into the registry payload. `dispatch_wave_status` includes per-item `live_token_count` and `live_context_pct` for items still `in_progress`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `uv run plugins/development-harness/scripts/claude_session_reader.py <session-id>` against a real `~/.claude/sessions/` directory. Output JSON has `token_count` (int), `context_window_pct` (float 0.0-1.0), `current_tool` (str|null), `last_message_at` (ISO timestamp). Reading triggers no writes to `~/.claude/`: `find ~/.claude -newer /tmp/marker` returns zero entries after invocation. Wired into `dispatch_wave_status` so its response shape gains `live_token_count` and `live_context_pct` fields for in-progress items.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"72f9bba135a311c206afc9bdb54c43b58608f0c943a732b35a23d8d5b89922cd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCwWcw\"}"}